{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Bela and Becher.</b> One should not dwell on their count. According to the chronicles, they turn out to be eleven, counting a brother (אח) in place of a sister (אחוה) — he is the brother mentioned here. One may answer that when they went down to Egypt they were only ten at the time of the descent, and afterward another was born; and the change of names is because he mentions him another time, and so is the practice throughout Scripture, when it comes to write — to mention what it has already mentioned." "<b>And Ard.</b> The vav with qamatz."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:47.577642731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}